                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "20134823",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198025704994",
                            "num_reviews": 104,
                            "playtime_forever": 303,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 303,
                            "last_played": 1451522056
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I got this from a greenlight bundle, and I must say I'm very happy with the game and the developer's response to issues I had with the game, making great improvements not long after I reported issues with the game. This is the kind of indie developer we need!\n\nRegarding the game itself, it is as fun and satisfying as the trailer makes you believe. Controller support is near perfect (it would be better if moving through menus did not require mouse emulation, as that makes the mouse curser appear in the middle of the screen), jumping is precise and the amount of challenge is good enough.\n\nThis is a very short game, but the bonus levels and level editor feature allow some extra gameplay time if you want more. It's definitely worth your time, and the dev really deserves your money!\n\nPros\n\n- Precise platforming\n- Fun\n- Fair puzzles\n- level editor\n- controller support works very well\n\nCons\n\n- Short (no problem for me, but some people want longer games)\n- music get repetitive after a while\n- had the game crash before being patched (works great now)",
